@731 = ~Ghost Weapon~
@732 = ~Ghost Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 3
Range: 0
Duration: 3 rounds / 2 levels
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: special
Saving Throw: none

A disarmed warlord can use Ghost Weapon to create a replacement. This spell shapes ether into a familiar weapon in the mage's hand. After that the weapon cannot leave his hand throughout the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped the same way. Such a weapon deals double weapon damage (a ghost long sword therefore inflicts 2D8 points of damage per hit) and penetrates defenses more readily, granting a +2 bonus to THAC0. The ghost weapon also inflicts 6 additional points of damage to undead that are particularly vulnerable to it.

Note: Do not create a two-handed sword or a halberd if you are equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, then remove your shield first.~
@73291 = ~Ghost Sword~
@73292 = ~Ghost Katana~
@73293 = ~Ghost Axe~
@73294 = ~Ghost Hammer~
@73295 = ~Ghost Flail~
@73296 = ~Ghost Halberd~
@73297 = ~Ghost Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 3
Range: 0
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: special
Saving Throw: none

A disarmed warlord can use Ghost Weapon to create a replacement. This spell shapes ether into a familiar weapon in the mage's hand. After that the weapon cannot leave his hand throughout the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped the same way. Such a weapon deals double weapon damage (a ghost long sword therefore inflicts 2D8 points of damage per hit) and penetrates defenses more readily, granting a +2 bonus to THAC0. The ghost weapon also inflicts 6 additional points of damage to undead that are particularly vulnerable to it.

Note: Do not create a two-handed sword or a halberd if you are equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, then remove your shield first.~
@73298 = ~Ghost Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 3
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

A warlord can use Ghost Weapon to create a weapon for the recipient. This spell shapes ether into a weapon in the recipient's hand, chosen by the warlord. He can only choose a weapon he knows how to use. After that the weapon cannot leave the hand of the recipient throughout the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped the same way. Such a weapon deals double weapon damage (a ghost long sword therefore inflicts 2D8 points of damage per hit) and penetrates defenses more readily, granting a +2 bonus to THAC0. The ghost weapon also inflicts 6 additional points of damage to undead that are particularly vulnerable to it.

Note: don't create a two-handed sword or a halberd if the recipient is equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, remove his shield first.~
@732981 = ~Ghost Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 3
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

A warlord can use Ghost Weapon to create a weapon for the recipient. This spell shapes ether into a weapon in the recipient's hand, chosen by the warlord. He can only choose a weapon he knows how to use. After that the weapon cannot leave the hand of the recipient throughout the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped the same way. Such a weapon deals double weapon damage (a ghost long sword therefore inflicts 2D8 points of damage per hit) and penetrates defenses more readily, granting a +2 bonus to THAC0. The ghost weapon also inflicts 6 additional points of damage to undead that are particularly vulnerable to it.

All allies within 5 meters of the target also benefit from reduced effects of the spell: the same weapon appears in their hands for 2 turns.

Note: Do not create a two-handed sword or a halberd if one of the recipients is equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, then remove the shields first.~

@733 = ~Armor of Fear~
@734 = ~Armor of Fear (Illusion, Enchantment)
Level: 3
Range: 0
Duration: 3 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: special

The spell surrounds the caster with a cloud of crackling black sparks, made of nightmares and torments. This dark armor generates fear by manifesting the deepest fears of the warlord's attackers. Thus, any opponent who hits the mage protected by the Armor of Fear faces his deepest fears and must make a successful save vs. spell or abandon the fight and flee for 1D4 rounds, terrified. The armor grows stronger with caster level, and every 3 experience levels beyond level 5 add a -1 penalty to saving throws and increase the duration of the illusion by 1 round.~
@7341 = ~Armor of Fear (Illusion, Enchantment)
Level: 3
Range: 0
Duration: 23 rounds
Casting Time: 2
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: special

The spell surrounds the caster with a cloud of crackling black sparks, made of nightmares and torments. This dark armor generates fear by manifesting the deepest fears of the warlord's attackers. Thus, any opponent who hits the mage protected by the Armor of Fear faces his deepest fears and must make a successful save vs. spell at -5 or abandon the fight and flee for 1D4 +5 rounds, terrified.~
@7342 = ~Armor of Fear (Illusion, Enchantment)
Level: 3
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 23 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

The spell surrounds the recipient with a cloud of crackling black sparks, made of nightmares and torments. This dark armor generates fear by manifesting the deepest fears of the wearer's attackers. Thus, any opponent who hits the recipient protected by the Armor of Fear faces his deepest fears and must make a successful save vs. spell at -5 or abandon the fight and flee for 1D4 +5 rounds, terrified.~
@73421 = ~Armor of Fear (Illusion, Enchantment)
Level: 3
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 23 rounds
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

The spell surrounds the recipient with a cloud of crackling black sparks, made of nightmares and torments. This dark armor generates fear by manifesting the deepest fears of the wearer's attackers. Thus, any opponent who hits the recipient protected by the Armor of Fear faces his deepest fears and must make a successful save vs. spell at -5 or abandon the fight and flee for 1D4 +5 rounds, terrified.

All allies within 5 meters of the target also benefit from reduced effects of the spell:
they are covered for 15 rounds by an armor that imposes a -3 penalty and makes enemies flee for 1D4 +3 rounds.~

@735 = ~Chameleon~
@736 = ~Chameleon (Illusion)
Level: 3
Range: 0
Duration: 3 rounds + 1 round / level
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

The warlord discovered this spell while seeking invisibility. The result is imperfect, but still useful.
Chameleon makes the warlord almost invisible. In fact, he is not really invisible but blends into the background by becoming transparent. He then gains a concealment bonus of +1 to AC and +1 to saving throws.
As long as he moves he can be spotted. But if he stops moving and stands still for 1 round, then he will really become invisible. He loses this advantage if he casts a spell or takes an offensive action, but remaining motionless for another round makes him invisible again. He can repeat this as often as desired while the spell lasts.~
